1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,958
Eyelid twitching all by itself?

2
00:00:01,958 --> 00:00:03,941
You’re not alone — it’s very common.

3
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:09,581
It’s called myokymia: tiny, involuntary flickers of the eyelid muscle.

4
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:13,182
1 — Stress: one of the most common triggers.

5
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:17,319
2 — Being tired and not sleeping enough.

6
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:22,481
3 — Too much caffeine: coffee, energy drinks.

7
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:27,002
4 — Eye strain from screens, and dry eyes.

8
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:31,174
It’s usually harmless and fades on its own.

9
00:00:31,174 --> 00:00:33,315
More sleep and less caffeine can help.

10
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:39,455
See a doctor if it lasts weeks, the eyelid fully closes, or other parts of the face twitch.
